# ============================================
# BACKEND SERVER CONFIGURATION (server.js)
# ============================================

# Azure Communication Services Email Configuration (Optional Primary Email Service)
# The system uses GoDaddy SMTP as the primary email service
# Azure Email Service can be configured as an optional primary, with GoDaddy SMTP as automatic fallback
# AZURE_EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS must be a verified email address in your Azure Communication Services domain
# If Azure Email fails or is unavailable, the system automatically falls back to GoDaddy SMTP
# Leave empty if you only want to use GoDaddy SMTP
AZURE_COMMUNICATION_SERVICES_CONNECTION_STRING=
AZURE_EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=support@oggaranefoods.com

# SMTP Configuration (GoDaddy Email Service)
# GoDaddy SMTP is used as the primary email service (with Azure Email as optional primary)
# This is the email account that will SEND emails on behalf of your website
# Anyone can still use the contact form - this is just the "from" address
SMTP_HOST=smtpout.secureserver.net
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=support@oggaranefoods.com
SMTP_PASS=your-godaddy-email-password

# Contact Email
# This is where contact form submissions will be DELIVERED
CONTACT_EMAIL=support@oggaranefoods.com

# Server Configuration
PORT=3001
NODE_ENV=development

# CORS Configuration (Backend)
# For production: Set your frontend domain(s) here, separated by commas
# Example: ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com,https://www.yourdomain.com
# For development: Leave empty to use default localhost origins
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# ============================================
# FRONTEND CONFIGURATION (.env or .env.production)
# ============================================
# Create a .env file in the root directory for development
# Create a .env.production file for production builds

# Backend URL (Frontend)
# For development: Leave empty to use default http://localhost:3001
# For production: Set to your backend server URL
# Example: VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com:3001
# Example: VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://your-ec2-ip:3001
VITE_BACKEND_URL=

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
#
# Email Service Configuration:
# The system uses GoDaddy SMTP as the primary email service
# - PRIMARY: GoDaddy SMTP (configured below) - support@oggaranefoods.com
# - OPTIONAL: Azure Communication Services Email (if configured above)
# If Azure Email is configured and fails, the system automatically falls back to GoDaddy SMTP
#
# GoDaddy SMTP Setup:
# 1. Use your GoDaddy email account: support@oggaranefoods.com
# 2. SMTP Server: smtpout.secureserver.net
# 3. Port: 465 (SSL) or 587 (STARTTLS) - 465 is recommended
# 4. Use your full email address as SMTP_USER: support@oggaranefoods.com
# 5. Use your GoDaddy email password as SMTP_PASS
# 6. Update CONTACT_EMAIL to support@oggaranefoods.com (where inquiries are received)
# 7. The system will automatically send confirmation emails to users mentioning 24-48 hour response time
#
# Azure Communication Services Email Setup (Optional):
# 1. Create an Azure account and navigate to Communication Services
# 2. Create a Communication Services resource in the Azure portal
# 3. Provision and verify an email domain in your Communication Services resource
# 4. Get your connection string from the Azure portal (Keys section)
# 5. Add AZURE_COMMUNICATION_SERVICES_CONNECTION_STRING above
# 6. Set AZURE_EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS to support@oggaranefoods.com
# 7. For detailed setup: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/communication-services/quickstarts/email/send-email
#
# Twilio WhatsApp Setup:
# 1. Create a Twilio project and enable WhatsApp (https://www.twilio.com/whatsapp)
# 2. Verify your business number or use the Twilio sandbox number
# 3. Add the sandbox/approved number as TWILIO_WHATSAPP_NUMBER (include whatsapp:+ prefix)
# 4. Copy Account SID and Auth Token into TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID / TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN
# 5. Expose your backend publicly and configure the webhook URL in the Twilio console to point at /whatsapp/webhook
# 6. (Optional) Set TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL if your server is behind a proxy and Twilio validation needs the canonical URL
#
# IMPORTANT: SMTP_USER is the account that SENDS emails, not who can USE the contact form.
# Anyone can fill out the contact form - this just determines which email account
# will be used to send the emails from your website.
#
# ============================================
# AWS EC2 DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
#
# 1. Copy this file to .env on your EC2 instance
# 2. Update SMTP credentials with your actual Gmail App Password
# 3. Set ALLOWED_ORIGINS to your frontend domain(s)
# 4. Create .env.production file with VITE_BACKEND_URL pointing to your backend
# 5. Build frontend: npm run build
# 6. Start backend: npm run server (or use PM2: pm2 start server.js)
# 7. Serve frontend: Use nginx or serve the dist folder
#
# Example .env.production:
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://your-ec2-private-ip:3001
# OR
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
